steinlens.fog.hint=Terrain distance fog. Light: only at the edge of the render distance. Water, lava and blindness don't change
steinlens.cloudHeight=Cloud height
steinlens.cloudHeight.blocks=+%s blocks
steinlens.cloudHeight.hint=Raises the cloud layer above the game's height (128)
steinlens.keep=Extended distance
steinlens.keep.memory=Memory
steinlens.keep.disk=Disk
steinlens.keep.hint=Chunks the server discards stay on screen up to your render distance. Disk: saved per server and world, they come back on the next visit (distant ones are a still image). Changing worlds clears the memory
steinlens.keepLimit=Storage limit
steinlens.keepLimit.hint=How much terrain to keep, in memory and on disk; past the limit, the farthest (memory) and oldest (disk) are removed first
steinlens.connectedTextures=Connected blocks
steinlens.connectedTextures.hint=Connected textures from the resource pack (glass, bookshelves...): %s rule(s)
steinlens.chunkUploads=Chunks per frame
steinlens.chunkUploads.hint=How many finished chunks go to the GPU per frame. With a limit, a burst of arriving chunks spreads over more frames: terrain appears more slowly, without stutters
steinlens.waitNeighbors=Wait for neighbors
steinlens.waitNeighbors.hint=Only builds a chunk once the 8 around it have arrived: one build per chunk instead of 3 to 5. The outer ring of loaded chunks is not shown
steinlens.directRender=Direct rendering
steinlens.directRender.hint=Draws straight to the window, without copying the game's intermediate image every frame. Turns off spectator and F4 shaders
